# A screw thread chosen from the list of sizes, left-handed, on an
# extruded circle; the same model as path_thread_choose.go makes
# (TestPathEquivalenceThreadChoose).
key c
move 300 300
down L 300 300
up L 300 300
move 350 300
down L 350 300
up L 350 300
key esc
key x shift
move 350 300
down L 350 300
up L 350 300
menu Features|Screw Thread...
# [choose] shows the series and the sizes of the thread's own.
twmove 271 110
twdown L 271 110
twup L 271 110
# Whitworth's sizes.
twmove 478 140
twdown L 478 140
twup L 478 140
# 1/2 BSW, then its fine pitch, BSF.
twmove 388 190
twdown L 388 190
twup L 388 190
twmove 253 260
twdown L 253 260
twup L 253 260
# Back to the thread, whose designation is now the one chosen.
twmove 55 290
twdown L 55 290
twup L 55 290
# Left-handed by a choice beside it, then made.
twmove 415 130
twdown L 415 130
twup L 415 130
# Flip the direction: against the circle's normal, down into the part.
twmove 60 230
twdown L 60 230
twup L 60 230
twmove 37 260
twdown L 37 260
twup L 37 260
